<o:LogicalDiagram Id="o98">
<a:ObjectID>FA47836B-688E-4841-81C8-96425C9E099F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Lease_Contract_Cost</a:Name>
<a:Code>LEASE_CONTRACT_COST</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1702381068</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Aled.Lewis</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1702992875</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Aled.Lewis</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A LEASE_CONTRACT will contain details of what needs to be paid (COSTs),
&gt; A LEASE_CONTRACT can contain multiple COSTs.
&gt; A COST can be allocated to multiple PARTNERs, this is set as a percentage of the COST in COST_ALLOCATION.

The details for each COST are determined in the LEASE_CONTRACT but are specific for each individual COST.
eg: A Partner may have multiple BANK_ACCOUNTs, multiple PAYMENT_METHODs etc registered but a COST can only be paid to one BANK_ACCOUNT using one PAYMENT_METHOD.

Whether there are IFRS16 requirements (FINANCIAL_REPORTING_STANDARDs), what the frequency of payment is (PAYMENT_FREQUENCY), how the COSTs should be grouped for Shall internal reporting (COST_OBJECT), which Taxes are applicable (TAX and WITHHOLDING_TAX) and what the COST is for (PAYMENT_TYPE) are determined in the LEASE_CONTRACT but are set specific to each COST.

Each time a COST is to be made a PAYMENT_TOKEN is created.
These PAYMENT_TOKENs are submitted to the relevant ERP for payment. (These are also known as Postings)</a:Comment>
