<o:LogicalDiagram Id="o155">
<a:ObjectID>0D7193B2-9152-4A27-B37A-5BFC5BA64397</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Lease_Contract_Payment_Token</a:Name>
<a:Code>LEASE_CONTRACT_PAYMENT_TOKEN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1702629967</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Aled.Lewis</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1702993338</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Aled.Lewis</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Once the COST data has determined that a payment needs to be made then a PAYMENT_TOKEN is created.
Each PAYMENT_TOKEN is submitted to a single ERP; the ERP which mastered the Vendor (PARTNER) from whom the property (LAND or BUILDING) is leased.
The PAYMENT_TOKEN contains all of the details which the ERP needs to make the payment; BANK,ACCOUNT, PAYMENT_METHOD, what the payment id for (COST), which Vendor is being paid (PARTNER) etc.
All of the details on the amonth to be paid, how the amount was calculated, for which time period the payment is for, which LEASE_CONTRACT the payment is for etc are contained within the PAYMENT_TOKEN itself.


Once a VENDOR_PAYMENT_TOKEN has been paid a LEDGER record is created which is the record of the financial transaction.
This LEDGER record is created in the ERP which arranged the payment.</a:Comment>
