<o:Entity Id="o340">
<a:ObjectID>6CE4E3CD-D33E-475F-9DD1-DE3494F33AB7</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Clause_Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>CLAUSE_TYP</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1702477170</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Aled.Lewis</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1744360917</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Nagavalli.Vinnakota</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Type of Clause, eg:
Lease Protection:   Lease Protection is used to indicate whether or not ell has Legal lease protection with Landlords or tenants – and whether or not either party is exempted from Lease Protection.  This could apply to Shell &amp; their Landlords, or with Shell tenants (i.e. on lease in or lease out contracts).
Notification Method : Means of communicating notifications to business partner.   This can be used by anyone (Legal Department Field Operators, PMC, PMA, etc) needing to send a legal notification, such as a contract renewal, termination, amendment, assignment or other legal communication.
Overhold:
Permitted Use:
Purchase Option:    An option in a lease agreement that allows the lesseo purchase the leased asset at the end of the lease period
Subletting:
Surrender/Restoration:
Volume Letter:      Volume Letter is used to indicate if there is a contual requirement to send a letter to Landlords certifying the final sales volume figures (this is not to be confused with the settlement letter with volumes).  This is an additional letter beyond the settlement letter</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{77894B2F-5C8A-41A3-AAF2-C1D07AC2DAD1},BIM-core,862={8DB6F0D8-502C-4315-805C-4AC30C42CB29},CommerciallySensitiveInformation,37=No Commercially Sensitive Information
