<o:Entity Id="o341">
<a:ObjectID>74CAFDDA-39B6-4D43-B247-E82B5394EEA9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Option_Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>OPTION_TYP</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1702477171</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Aled.Lewis</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1744360917</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Nagavalli.Vinnakota</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Type of the Option, eg:
Notice End: Rule determining the end date notice can be given prior to the contract end
Automatic Renewal:  Contract will be continuous/evergreen
Option to Purchase Contract:
Purchase Option:    An option in a lease agreement that allows the lesseo purchase the leased asset at the end of the lease period
Renewal Option:     A clause in a lease that outlines the terms for reneg or extending an original lease agreement. The renewal option appears as a covenant in the original lease and provides specifications under which the leaseholder can renew or extend the original lease term for an additional, specified time and rate (rent).
Termination Option: A clause in a lease that outlines the terms for ending an original lease agreement. the original lease term for an additional, specified time and rate (rent).</a:Comment>
